.\n3. **A hit turns the blob into 2.** When the beam reaches a 1 cell, that whole blob is recoloured 2.\n4. **The marker redirects the beam.** The blob's 3 marker also becomes 2. The beam then leaves through the marker, travelling away from the blob, and it is as wide as the marker (2 cells).\n   - Pair 2: the beam enters the lower blob, leaves upward through the top marker at columns 9–10, and hits the next blob.\n   - That blob's marker is on its right, so the beam turns right along rows 4–5.\n   - It hits a third blob whose marker is on top, so it exits upward at columns 19–20 to the border.\n5. **The beam stops where the edge or a blob is.** It keeps going until it hits another 1 cell or leaves the grid.\n6. **Everything the beam did not touch is erased.** Blobs and markers the beam never reached become 8. Only 2 remains in the output.\n\n**How the direction is read.** The exit direction is the side of the blob's bounding box on which the marker lies (above, below, left or right). The marker belonging to a blob is the 3 component that touches the blob (8-neighbour adjacency).\n\n**Applying it to the test.** The beam rises from (23,5).\n- It hits the big blob (rows 2–9, columns 1–8), whose marker is on its right at rows 5–6, so the beam goes right along rows 5–6.\n- It hits the blob at rows 4–8, columns 14–19. Its marker is on top at columns 16–17, so the beam goes up to the top border.\n- The lower-right blob is never reached and is erased.\n\n**Teaching stages emitted by the program.**\n- The launcher's 4 is first turned into 2.\n- Then each beam segment is emitted, together with the blob it converts.\n- Finally the grid is emitted after the untouched blobs and markers are cleaned up.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = 8\n    out = g.copy()\n    # launcher\n    fy, fx = [tuple(p) for p in np.argwhere(g == 4)][0]\n    d = (-1, 0)\n    for dy, dx in [(1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)]:\n        y, x = fy+dy, fx+dx\n        if 0 <= y < H and 0 <= x < W and g[y, x] == 2:\n            d = (-dy, -dx)\n    out[fy, fx] = 2\n    emit(out, \"Launcher 4 becomes part of the 2 beam; beam fires away from its tail.\")\n    blobs = components(g == 1)\n    marks = components(g == 3)\n    blob_id = {}\n    for i, b in enumerate(blobs):\n        for c in b:\n            blob_id[c] = i\n    front = [(fy, fx)]\n    used = set()\n    while True:\n        hit = None\n        while True:\n            nxt = [(y+d[0], x+d[1]) for y, x in front]\n            if any(not (0 <= y < H and 0 <= x < W) for y, x in nxt):\n                break\n            hs = [blob_id[c] for c in nxt if c in blob_id]\n            if hs:\n                hit = hs[0]\n                break\n            for y, x in nxt:\n                out[y, x] = 2\n            front = nxt\n        if hit is None or hit in used:\n            emit(out, \"Beam travels straight until it leaves the grid.\")\n            break\n        used.add(hit)\n        b = blobs[hit]\n        for y, x in b:\n            out[y, x] = 2\n        bs = set(b)\n        mk = None\n        for m in marks:\n            if any((y+a, x+c) in bs for y, x in m for a in (-1,0,1) for c in (-1,0,1)):\n                mk = m\n                break\n        if mk is None:\n            emit(out, \"Beam hits a blob with no marker and stops.\")\n            break\n        for y, x in mk:\n            out[y, x] = 2\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(b)\n        my, mx = mk[0]\n        if my < y0: d = (-1, 0)\n        elif my > y1: d = (1, 0)\n        elif mx < x0: d = (0, -1)\n        else: d = (0, 1)\n        front = list(mk)\n        emit(out, \"Beam hits a blob: blob and its 3 marker turn 2; beam exits through the marker.\")\n    out[out != 2] = bg\n    emit(out, \"Erase all blobs and markers the beam never reached.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**A hit turns the blob into 2.** When the beam reaches a 1 cell, that whole blob is recoloured 2."}],"rays":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- a launcher: a single 4 cell with a short tail of 2s behind it;"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**The launcher fires a beam.** The 4 fires a 1-cell-wide beam of 2, pointing away from its tail."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In every pair the tail is below the 4, so the beam goes up."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**How the direction is read.** The exit direction is the side of the blob's bounding box on which the marker lies (above, below, left or right)."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- It hits a third blob whose marker is on top, so it exits upward at columns 19–20 to the border."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Its marker is on top at columns 16–17, so the beam goes up to the top border."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"b1578fd9d8135cecbb8fb10f76755fc644d47389ee8fd3a86c4e6302ecf63eba","task_sha256":"92a9ecd545a741a492fbf88843582c4a83d2e567aaca16258c103a5ec9ce0c1c","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
